course: dictionary
lesson: 3154
title: Emerge: coming out into view
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Emerge means to come out from inside or behind something so that people can see it. «A chick emerged from the egg.» The clue is «from the egg»: the chick was inside, and now it is out where we can see it.
explain: Emerge can also mean to become known, or to appear slowly over time. «The truth emerged later.» Nobody knew at first. As time passed, the facts came out. Ask yourself: what came out, or what became clear?
explain: Emerge can mean to come through a hard time. «She emerged from the illness stronger.» The word stronger is the clue: she came out the other side. Check with a swap: "She came out of the illness stronger" still makes sense, so emerge means the same here.
fact: Emerge means to come out, or to become seen or known.
fact: «Emerged» is the past tense: «The butterfly emerged from its cocoon.»
fact: «Emerging» is the -ing form: «A new plan is emerging.»
fact: Useful phrases are «emerge from» and «it emerged that…», as in «It emerged that the bridge was closed.»
fact: Emerge is a verb, so it describes an action. Its forms are emerge, emerges, emerged and emerging.
exercise: «The bear emerged from the dark cave, blinking in the sunlight.» What does emerged mean? | Hid behind a tree | Fell fast asleep | *Came out from inside into view | Ran away from the sun
exercise: «It emerged that the shop had been closed all week.» What does emerged mean here? | Started raining | Moved quickly | *Became known | Was painted green
exercise: Which word in «Tiny shoots emerged from the soil after the rain» tells you the shoots came up out of the ground? | after | rain | Tiny | *emerged
test: «A new idea emerged during the meeting.» What does emerged mean? | Was thrown away | Ended suddenly | Was measured carefully | *Appeared, or was first thought of
test: Yasmin says «emerging» means the same as «hiding». Why is she wrong? | They mean exactly the same, so there is no difference | *Emerging means coming out into view, the opposite of hiding | Emerging means being very tired | Emerging means hiding inside something
exam: What is the best swap for emerged in «New ideas emerged from the discussion»? | *appeared | hid | slept | sank
